From c5cce5641a1bd8f1f48f53f39317799b231635fc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 18:53:19 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] fix(sim): the floor read refuses any column a tool came
 within a cell of

Review of #649: floor_at read only the floor point's own cell and
counted it cut only when that cell's CENTRE was inside the tool, so a
point inside a cut within half a cell of its wall (and a cut thinner
than a cell) read the uncut shell floor. It now refuses when the swept
tool came within one cell of any centre in the 3x3x3 block around the
floor point (claim > -cell) - conservative, the safe direction. Docs
say exact 'to rounding'.

Pinned by field_floor::a_point_inside_a_cut_near_its_wall_is_refused_too
(y 3.81 .. 8.19 inside an r 2.2 slot, the review's repro).

Refs #637

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX
